# Controlled Tool Agent

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:runic_ai, path: "~/wrk/runic_ai"}
])

Code.require_file("support/runic_ai_livebook.exs", __DIR__)
```

## Purpose

Tool use needs control points. A model may request a capability, but your
workflow decides whether the capability should run, wait, be reviewed, be
rewritten, or halt.

`RunicAI.Recipes.GuardedOperatorToolAgent` adds:

* budget checks before tool execution and answer commitment
* guard checks at `:pre_tool` and `:pre_answer`
* `ReviewRequest` pause points
* `Wait` pause points
* retry and fallback around generation
* resume via `ReviewDecision` or `ResumeSignal`

## Provider Setup

```elixir
setup = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.inputs()
```

```elixir
model = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_model!(setup)
llm_opts = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.llm_opts(model, max_output_tokens: RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_max_output_tokens(setup))
```

## Define A Privileged Tool

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Tool.Definition

refund_tool =
  Definition.new!(
    name: "issue_refund",
    description: "Issue a demo refund for an order. This is a privileged action.",
    parameter_schema: %{
      "type" => "object",
      "additionalProperties" => false,
      "required" => ["order_id", "amount_usd", "reason"],
      "properties" => %{
        "order_id" => %{"type" => "string"},
        "amount_usd" => %{"type" => "number"},
        "reason" => %{"type" => "string"}
      }
    },
    executor: fn args ->
      amount = Map.get(args, :amount_usd) || Map.get(args, "amount_usd")

      {:ok,
       %{
         order_id: Map.get(args, :order_id) || Map.get(args, "order_id"),
         amount_usd: amount / 1,
         reason: Map.get(args, :reason) || Map.get(args, "reason"),
         status: "refund queued in demo ledger"
       }}
    end
  )
```

```elixir
single_tool_batch = RunicAI.Livebook.Tools.once_per_loop_selector()
```

## Visualize The Controlled Workflow

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Recipes.GuardedOperatorToolAgent

controlled_workflow =
  GuardedOperatorToolAgent.new(
    model: model,
    registry: [refund_tool],
    tool_selector: single_tool_batch,
    tool_requirement: :required,
    pre_tool_guard: fn _guard_request -> :review end,
    llm_opts: llm_opts
  )

RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(controlled_workflow)
```

## Pause Before The Tool Runs

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.require_openai_key!()

paused =
  GuardedOperatorToolAgent.react_until_resolution(
    [
      model: model,
      registry: [refund_tool],
      tool_selector: single_tool_batch,
      tool_requirement: :required,
      pre_tool_guard: fn _guard_request -> :review end,
      llm_opts: llm_opts
    ],
    %{
      user: "Issue a $12 refund for order A-100 because the package arrived late."
    }
  )

GuardedOperatorToolAgent.latest_review_request(paused)
```

```elixir
Kino.Layout.tabs(
  "Pending state": Kino.Tree.new(GuardedOperatorToolAgent.latest_state(paused)),
  "Review request": Kino.Tree.new(GuardedOperatorToolAgent.latest_review_request(paused)),
  "Tool results": Kino.Tree.new(GuardedOperatorToolAgent.latest_tool_results(paused))
)
```

## Approve And Resume

```elixir
review_request = GuardedOperatorToolAgent.latest_review_request(paused)
paused_state = GuardedOperatorToolAgent.latest_state(paused)

resumed =
  GuardedOperatorToolAgent.react_until_resolution(
    [
      model: model,
      registry: [refund_tool],
      tool_selector: single_tool_batch,
      tool_requirement: :required,
      pre_tool_guard: fn _guard_request -> :review end,
      llm_opts: llm_opts
    ],
    %{
      state: paused_state,
      review_decision: %{resume_key: review_request.resume_key, status: :approved}
    }
  )

GuardedOperatorToolAgent.latest_reply_text(resumed)
```

## Interactive HITL Agent

Submit a refund request in the Message tab. When the review request appears,
switch to the Review tab and submit `approved`, `edited`, or `rejected`.

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Chat.start(
  GuardedOperatorToolAgent,
  [
    model: model,
    registry: [refund_tool],
    tool_selector: single_tool_batch,
    tool_requirement: :required,
    pre_tool_guard: fn _guard_request -> :review end,
    llm_opts: llm_opts
  ],
  initial_message: "Please refund order A-100 for $12 because it arrived late."
)
```

## Design Takeaway

The model can propose. The workflow authorizes. That boundary is what lets you
use tools for real application capabilities without treating generated text as
permission.
